  "query_preview": "(Monday through Thursday)...\nLow pressure near the California will weaken early next week. High\npressure to the east may begin to expand across the area for the\nlatter half of next week. Temperatures will continue to cool for\nearly next week with Tuesday high temperatures ranging from the\n70s near the coast to the 80s for the Inland Empire with the lower\ndeserts around 100. This will be followed by a warming trend for\nWednesday through Friday of next week, but with increase spread \nin just how much warming may occur. The NBM 50th percentile would \nwarm temperatures to around average for Friday of next week with\nhigh temperatures for next Friday ranging from the mid 70s to\nlower 80s near the coast to the upper 80s and lower 90s for the\nInland Empire with 100 to 104 for the lower deserts. Dry weather \nis expected to continue for Monday through Thursday of next week.",
